Description: opt in to Qt private module loading for Qt >= 6.9
 kwayland links Qt6::WaylandClientPrivate. Since Qt 6.9 (and in 6.12),
 the private module counterpart is no longer loaded automatically when
 finding the public package: Qt6WaylandClientConfig.cmake only calls
 find_package(Qt6WaylandClientPrivate) when QT_FIND_PRIVATE_MODULES is
 set. Without this flag CMake generation fails with:
 .
   Target "KWaylandClient" links to: Qt6::WaylandClientPrivate
   but the target was not found.
 .
 Set QT_FIND_PRIVATE_MODULES before the first find_package(Qt6*) call.
 The flag is a no-op on older Qt versions.
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-04

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -42,6 +42,10 @@
                         PACKAGE_VERSION_FILE "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/KWaylandConfigVersion.cmake"
                         SOVERSION 6)
 
 # Dependencies
+# Qt >= 6.9 does not auto-load private module counterparts unless the
+# consumer opts in; needed for the Qt6::WaylandClientPrivate target.
+set(QT_FIND_PRIVATE_MODULES ON)
 find_package(Qt6Gui ${QT_MIN_VERSION} REQUIRED NO_MODULE COMPONENTS Private)
 find_package(Qt6 ${QT_MIN_VERSION} CONFIG REQUIRED Concurrent)
 find_package(Qt6WaylandClient ${QT_MIN_VERSION} CONFIG REQUIRED NO_MODULE COMPONENTS Private)
